URL: https://ftp.fau.de/pub/OpenBSD/OpenSSH/portable/openssh-10.6p1.tar.gz 5b27910392630fe98eaef74e2ed72ad3416e108ee4234f1be7228c681e515137
Origname: openssh-10.6p1
Name: openssh

    OpenSSH for Fil-C, based on upstream 10.6p1. Patch provenance:
    (1) GSSAPI key exchange from openssh-gsskex (github.com/openssh-gsskex/openssh-gsskex, debian/master lineage), rebased onto 10.6p1 per Debian's src:ssh-team/openssh-gssapi gssapi.patch for 10.6p1, and carrying their CVE-2026-3497-lineage hardening: ssh_packet_disconnect() (which flushes and fatals) instead of sshpkt_disconnect() (which merely queues) at every protocol-violation site in kexgssc.c and kexgsss.c, GSS_C_EMPTY_BUFFER initialization of every gss_buffer_desc local that error paths release, the kex_gss_c25519_client() bounds fix against a 1-byte overread of an empty server_blob, and upstream 10.6's GSSAPI credential-store security fix (ssh_gssapi_storecreds() gated on gssapi_client.userok, new ssh_gssapi_cleanup_global_client() called from mm_answer_gss_setup_ctx() and from the failed-userok path, the userok field replacing used).
    (2) GSS_KEX_DEFAULT_KEX hardened to drop the deprecated SHA1 methods (gss-group14-sha1-, gss-gex-sha1-) per Debian/Ubuntu; they stay available when explicitly configured, and the GSSAPIKexAlgorithms default text in ssh_config.5/sshd_config.5 was updated to match.
    (3) mlkem1024nistp384-sha384 hybrid from Fedora's 0047-NIST-curves-hybrid-KEX, moderated per djb feedback: upstream PQ implementations are kept, there are no FIPS changes (we build no FIPS OpenSSL), and the mlkem+nistp kexes are NOT added to the default KEX proposal lists (myproposal.h stays byte-identical to upstream; they remain name-valid and configurable); Fedora's server_key NULL-check fix in kex_kem_mlkem_nist_enc() is kept, and our added default: case in kex_kem_mlkem_nist_dec() sets SSH_ERR_SIGNATURE_INVALID instead of returning an uninitialized r.
    (4) systemd socket activation from Ubuntu's openssh socket-activation patch (Steve Langasek lineage): LISTEN_PID/LISTEN_FDS handling, setup_systemd_socket() for AF_INET/AF_INET6/AF_VSOCK with FD_CLOEXEC clearing, listen_socks_no_close[], close_listen_socks(force), the -N re-exec argument, REEXEC_* fd offsets shifted by the systemd fd count, and AC_DEFINE(SYSTEMD_SOCKET_ACTIVATION).
    (5) Debian bug #1091820 fix (HostKey none + GSS kex): keep ext-info-s/kex-strict-s signalling and avoid freeing a string literal (hkalgs_prop in kex_proposal_populate_entries(), the xstrdup("null") host-key proposal).
    (6) Fil-C-specific fixes: zsetproctitle() runtime builtin in openbsd-compat/setproctitle.c, and seccomp sandbox zlock_runtime_threads()/sched_yield/MAP_NORESERVE/SECCOMP_RET_KILL_PROCESS.
    (7) configure and config.h.in regenerated with autoconf 2.71 (the version upstream used), adding SYSTEMD_SOCKET_ACTIVATION.
    (8) Excluded on purpose: Fedora's FIPS/libcrux plumbing, adding the mlkem+nistp kexes to the default lists, and a vestigial whitespace-only sntrup761.c hunk (sntrup761.c stays byte-identical to upstream), and a dead #include <stdfil.h> in kexmlkem768x25519.c (the file uses no stdfil.h symbols).
